    {
      "title": "Module 1 \u00b7 Differentiation from First Principles",
      "html": "$$f'(x)=\\lim_{h\\to 0}\\dfrac{f(x+h)-f(x)}{h}$$<p>Apply the formula, simplify, then let $h\\to 0$.</p><h4>Key points</h4><ul><li>Power rule: $\\dfrac{dy}{dx} = n\\cdot x^{n-1} = 2x^{1}$.</li><li>Power rule: $\\dfrac{dy}{dx} = n\\cdot x^{n-1} = 3x^{2}$.</li></ul><h4>Worked example</h4><p><b>Q:</b> Differentiate $y = x^{2}$ with respect to $x$.<br/><b>A:</b> 2x^{1}</p><p><b>Q:</b> Differentiate $y = x^{3}$ with respect to $x$.<br/><b>A:</b> 3x^{2}</p>",
      "examples": [
        {
          "q": "Find $f'(x)$ if $f(x)=x^2$ from first principles.",
          "a": "$\\dfrac{(x+h)^2 - x^2}{h} = \\dfrac{2xh + h^2}{h} = 2x + h$. As $h\\to 0$: $f'(x)=2x$."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "title": "Module 2 \u00b7 Rules of Differentiation",
      "html": "<ul><li>Power rule: $\\dfrac{d}{dx}(x^n) = nx^{n-1}$.</li><li>Constant rule: $\\dfrac{d}{dx}(c) = 0$.</li><li>Sum rule: derivative of a sum is the sum of the derivatives.</li></ul><h4>Key points</h4><ul><li>Power rule: $\\dfrac{dy}{dx} = n\\cdot x^{n-1} = 2x^{1}$.</li><li>Power rule: $\\dfrac{dy}{dx} = n\\cdot x^{n-1} = 3x^{2}$.</li></ul><h4>Worked example</h4><p><b>Q:</b> Differentiate $y = x^{2}$ with respect to $x$.<br/><b>A:</b> 2x^{1}</p><p><b>Q:</b> Differentiate $y = x^{3}$ with respect to $x$.<br/><b>A:</b> 3x^{2}</p>",
      "examples": [
        {
          "q": "Differentiate $y=3x^4 - 5x^2 + 7$.",
          "a": "$\\dfrac{dy}{dx} = 12x^3 - 10x$."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "title": "Module 3 \u00b7 Integration & Area",
      "html": "$$\\int x^n\\,dx = \\dfrac{x^{n+1}}{n+1} + C\\ (n\\ne -1)$$<p>The area under $y=f(x)$ between $x=a$ and $x=b$ (where $f\\ge 0$) is $\\int_a^b f(x)\\,dx$.</p><h4>Key points</h4><ul><li>$\\int_0^5 x^2 dx = \\left[\\dfrac{x^{3}}{3}\\right]_0^5 = \\dfrac{5^{3}}{3} = 125/3$.</li><li>$\\int_0^5 x^3 dx = \\left[\\dfrac{x^{4}}{4}\\right]_0^5 = \\dfrac{5^{4}}{4} = 625/4$.</li></ul><h4>Worked example</h4><p><b>Q:</b> Find the area under $y = x^{2}$ from $x = 0$ to $x = 5$.<br/><b>A:</b> \\dfrac{125}{3} \\text{ sq units}</p><p><b>Q:</b> Find the area under $y = x^{3}$ from $x = 0$ to $x = 5$.<br/><b>A:</b> \\dfrac{625}{4} \\text{ sq units}</p><h4>More key points</h4><ul><li>Find the area under $y = x^{2}$ from $x = 0$ to $x = 5$. \u2014 \\dfrac{125}{3} \\text{ sq units}.</li><li>Find the area under $y = x^{3}$ from $x = 0$ to $x = 5$. \u2014 \\dfrac{625}{4} \\text{ sq units}.</li><li>Find the area under $y = x^{2}$ from $x = 0$ to $x = 4$. \u2014 \\dfrac{64}{3} \\text{ sq units}.</li><li>Find the area under $y = x^{1}$ from $x = 0$ to $x = 4$. \u2014 8 \\text{ sq units}.</li></ul>",
      "examples": [
        {
          "q": "Evaluate $\\int (2x+3)\\,dx$.",
          "a": "$x^2 + 3x + C$."
        },
        {
          "q": "Find the area under $y=x^2$ from $x=0$ to $x=2$.",
          "a": "$\\int_0^2 x^2 dx = [x^3/3]_0^2 = 8/3$ square units."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "title": "Differentiation of algebraic functions",
      "html": "<p><b>Differentiation of algebraic functions</b> is a key part of Introductory Calculus (SSS 3, Mathematics). Master the meaning, the main points and how it is tested in JAMB and WAEC questions on this topic.</p><h4>Key points</h4><ul><li>Learn the meaning of differentiation of algebraic functions and the terms used with it.</li><li>Know the main types, features or steps involved in differentiation of algebraic functions.</li><li>Be able to give an example of differentiation of algebraic functions and explain why it matters in introductory calculus.</li><li>Practise past questions on differentiation of algebraic functions until you can answer them without notes.</li></ul><h4>Worked example</h4><p><b>Q:</b> Differentiate $y = x^{2}$ with respect to $x$.<br/><b>A:</b> 2x^{1} \u2014 Power rule: $\\dfrac{dy}{dx} = n\\cdot x^{n-1} = 2x^{1}$.</p><p><b>Q:</b> Differentiate $y = x^{3}$ with respect to $x$.<br/><b>A:</b> 3x^{2} \u2014 Power rule: $\\dfrac{dy}{dx} = n\\cdot x^{n-1} = 3x^{2}$.</p>",
      "examples": [
        {
          "q": "Differentiate $y = x^{2}$ with respect to $x$.",
          "a": "2x^{1} \u2014 Power rule: $\\dfrac{dy}{dx} = n\\cdot x^{n-1} = 2x^{1}$."
        },
        {
          "q": "Differentiate $y = x^{3}$ with respect to $x$.",
          "a": "3x^{2} \u2014 Power rule: $\\dfrac{dy}{dx} = n\\cdot x^{n-1} = 3x^{2}$."
        }
      ]
    },
